    <string name="tips_title">Wake up with one alarm</string>
    <string name="tips_body">"This app is built to make sure a single alarm actually wakes you — but the science says the alarm is only half the job:\n\n• Sleep in 90-minute cycles. Waking mid-cycle feels awful; waking at the end feels natural. Try for a total sleep time that\'s a multiple of 90 minutes (6h, 7.5h, 9h).\n\n• Snoozing restarts your sleep cycle, then yanks you out of it minutes later — that\'s what causes grogginess, not the wake-up itself. This app has no snooze: it keeps ringing until you solve a math question.\n\n• Keep your wake time fixed, even on weekends. Your body clock will start waking you up on its own a few minutes early.\n\n• The moment you\'re up, get bright light and a glass of water — both cut morning grogginess more than people expect.\n\n• Give yourself a reason to get up: coffee, a podcast, a few quiet minutes before the day starts."</string>
